    "notes": "Both claims verified against their own abstracts. Side A correctly extracts the short-term subgroup result (WMD -1.18; 95% CI -2.32, -0.04; P=0.04; 'was effective for weight loss'), a directional between-group effect favoring LCD. Side B correctly extracts the authors' reported weight result ('did not differ significantly between groups'), coded as explicit_no_difference, which is consistent with the authors' substantive conclusion that carbohydrate quantity 'is not an important determinant of response to dietary management'. Exposure (LCD vs higher/normal-carbohydrate diet), population (type 2 diabetes), outcome (body weight/weight change) and contrast (between-group) are sufficiently similar across the two meta-analyses. Side A's finding is a short-term duration subgroup while Side B reports the overall weight result from trials of >=3 months; this is retained as context but does not block comparison, and no text-supported explanatory difference is claimed."
